    },
    {
     "code": "A1",
     "for": "$x = 1$ and $x = 6$",
     "notes": "Both values needed. The $y$-coordinates $2$ and $7$ are not required for this mark."
    },
    {
     "code": "M1",
     "for": "Integrates (curve $-$ line), i.e. $\\int (-x^2 + 7x - 6)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, with at least one power of $x$ increased by 1, e.g. $-\\frac{x^3}{3} + \\frac{7x^2}{2} - 6x$",
     "notes": "Also allow integrating $C$ and $l$ separately and subtracting. Integrating (line $-$ curve) earns this M only if the student then takes the modulus with a clear reason."
