   "solution": [
    {
     "step": 1,
     "working": "$-x^2 + 8x - 5 = x + 1 \\Rightarrow x^2 - 7x + 6 = 0 \\Rightarrow (x - 1)(x - 6) = 0$",
     "mark": "M1"
    },
    {
     "step": 2,
     "working": "$x = 1$ or $x = 6$. Between these values, e.g. at $x = 2$, the curve gives $7$ and the line gives $3$, so $C$ is above $l$.",
     "mark": "A1"
    },
    {
     "step": 3,
     "working": "Area $= \\int_1^6 \\left[(-x^2 + 8x - 5) - (x + 1)\\right]\\mathrm{d}x = \\int_1^6 (-x^2 + 7x - 6)\\,\\mathrm{d}x = \\left[-\\frac{x^3}{3} + \\frac{7x^2}{2} - 6x\\right]_1^6$",
     "mark": "M1"
    },
    {
     "step": 4,
     "working": "$= \\left(-72 + 126 - 36\\right) - \\left(-\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{7}{2} - 6\\right) = 18 - \\left(-\\frac{17}{6}\\right)$",
     "mark": "dM1"
    },
    {
     "step": 5,
     "working": "$= \\frac{108}{6} + \\frac{17}{6} = \\frac{125}{6}$ as required.",
     "mark": "A1*"
    }
